[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The two plates are arranged in a 3/4 overhead perspective at a 40-degree angle, with the primary serving in sharp focus and the second plate slightly blurred in the background, ensuring all components are clearly visible. The camera captures a shallow depth of field with soft, natural side lighting from a window on the left, casting gentle, realistic shadows. The setting features a rustic, aged oak tabletop with slight wood grain textures. One simple, matte ceramic plate sits beside a rumpled, neutral-toned linen napkin and a scattered few fresh dill fronds and a halved, squeezed lemon. The salmon fillet is placed at the center, coated in a glistening mustard-dill glaze with visible whole-grain mustard seeds and bright green specks of chopped dill; the flesh is a pale, flaky coral pink. Resting to one side of the fish, not atop it, are crisp, golden-brown roasted baby potato cubes with caramelized edges and seasoned with flecks of garlic powder and black pepper. Beside the potatoes, bright, tender-crisp green beans add a fresh color contrast. Toasted almond slivers are scattered over the salmon and beans. The scene includes minor, authentic imperfections: a tiny sauce drip on the plate edge and a few loose crumbs, conveying a home-cooked, lived-in feel. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No plastic sheen, no symmetry, no hands, no text, no watermarks, indistinguishable from professional cookbook editorial photography."
]
